Subject: [PATCH 013/230] Add a dev-only demo dataset behind a production guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A fresh checkout had 32 users, no predictions, no ratings and empty
leaderboards, which made it impossible to judge whether a screen worked
or merely looked idle.

The seed writes through the real scoring path — points come from
scoreLineup and land in the ledger via award() — so the demo board cannot
disagree with the one a real user would be ranked on. It attaches
predictions to synced fixtures instead of inventing teams or athletes, and
mints no credentials, so demo accounts are reachable only through the
dev-token path that production already refuses to boot with.

assertNotProduction() throws before the first query runs, and --reset
deletes only the 9000NN id range, so neither can touch real data.

